    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d714">

                <pb facs="0595" n="479" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg479"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/11677.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Chargé d’Affaires
                        to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 134.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexican Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 21, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: At half past nine to-day I had the
                    honor to receive from His Excellency the Provisional Constitutional President of
                    the United Mexican States, General Victoriano Huerta, a telegram as follows:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>We are fighting at Vera Cruz against the unlawful landing of American
                            marines.</p>
                        <p>In the name of the Government that you represent, bring this fact to the
                            attention of whom it may concern.</p>
                        <p>Acknowledge receipt of this cable.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>In bringing the foregoing to the attention of your excellency I renew [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Algara E. de Terreros</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
